::kind(fixture)

// A macro whose body is `[ ... ]` is a block macro: where a string macro gives
// text, it gives the blocks, with `${1}` and `${name}` filled in.
::macros{
  card: [ @card(title: ${1})[ ${2} ] ]
  notice: [ Notice: ${msg} ]
  plain: "https://example.com/${1}"
}

=[ ブロックマクロ ]

${macro.card("Welcome", "Hello from a block macro")}

${macro.notice(msg: "Important")}

文章の中の ${macro.notice(msg: "ここ")} にも置ける。

文字列のマクロは今までどおり: ${macro.plain("x")}
